<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adad-nirari II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 911–891 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adad-nirari II was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> from 911 to 891 BCE and is counted as the first king of the Neo-Assyrian period. He campaigned against the Aramaean states of upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, collecting tribute from rulers along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khabur-river">Khabur</a>, and fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a>, recovering territory and fixing a border by treaty. His wars began the long recovery of Assyrian power.</p></div>
